// LLD of the check namespace (ds::check): the bound model resolved and checked.
// Every reference resolves outward through its scopes and then the extern
// catalogue; what nobody declares becomes an expected node reported once;
// behaviours are unified under their subject and checked against the static
// context (SREQ-00002-1, SREQ-00004-1).

package driftspec@ds {

  module check {

    requirement REQ-00010-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00002-1
      title: The checker shall resolve every reference outward through its scopes and report every incoherence as a finding at its location
      text:
        A name resolves in the innermost scope first, then outward one scope
        at a time, then in the extern catalogue by simple name; a full
        identity resolves directly; an artefact link resolves to the declared
        revision and reports W-REVISION-DRIFT when it names another. What
        nobody declares becomes an expected node, reported once as
        W-REF-UNDECLARED. Template arguments are checked against their bound,
        ownership against cycles, operators against their declaration,
        verifications against their tests, approved requirements against
        their verifications. Interfaces, abstract classes and value types are
        classified from the members.
      rationale:
        The tool's value is saying where the model contradicts itself,
        without stopping at the first problem and without refusing a
        workspace that is still being written.
      tags: check, resolution
    }

    requirement REQ-00011-1 {
      status: approved
      @refines SREQ-00004-1
      title: The checker shall identify every behaviour by its resolved subject and check its messages and events against the static context
      text:
        A sequence or state machine bound under the subject as written is
        renamed to the resolved subject, so two files describing one method
        meet in one behaviour and a scenario declared twice is a duplicate.
        A message is checked against the operation it names on the type of
        its target and against its arity; an event or action must be an
        operation of its entity; a local or attribute typed in another module
        is coupling, structural or transient.
      rationale:
        Bound by identity, the behaviour is checked like the rest of the
        model and the abstraction level of a diagram comes from the
        architecture instead of from the author.
      tags: check, behaviour
    }

    verification VER-00010-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00010-1
      title: Unit tests cover resolution order, expected nodes, the static oracle and the artefact oracle
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.UndeclaredReferencesBecomeExpectedNodesReportedOnce
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.ResolvesInnermostScopeFirst
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.MessagesToExpectedTypesAreNotReportedTwice
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.ExternDeclaresIdentitiesWithoutObligations
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.InterfaceAndAbstractAreDerived
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.EnumsAndTemplatesHaveIdentities
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.OwnershipAndMultiplicityComeFromTheAttribute
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.OperatorsAreDeclaredInTheHeaderAndRefinedInTheBody
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.CrossModuleReferencesNeedTheModuleNotAnInclude
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheRevisionIsPartOfTheIdentityAndLinksNameIt
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.LevelByPlacementAndNestingGivesTheRelation
        tests/unit/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.ABareNameFallsBackToTheExternCatalogue
    }

    verification VER-00011-1 {
      status: approved
      @requirement REQ-00011-1
      title: Unit tests cover the behaviour oracle, identity by subject, participants, expansion, coupling and state events
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.TheOracleFindings
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.ABehaviourIsIdentifiedByItsSubject
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.ParticipantsComeFromTheStaticContext
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.AMessageToAnOperationWithABehaviourExpandsToIt
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.CouplingIsDerivedFromWhatABehaviourTouchesOutsideItsModule
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.StateEventsAndActionsAreOperations
        tests/unit/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.AStateEventMustBeAnOperationOfItsEntity
    }

    class Checker {
      @requirement REQ-00010-1
      @requirement REQ-00011-1
      - owns renamed_: std::map<std::string, std::string>
      - refs model_: model::Model
      - owns reported_: std::set<std::string>
      + Checker(model: model::Model)
      + run(binder: bind::Binder) -> void
      + resolve(name: std::string, scope: std::string) -> std::string
      + externsNamed(name: std::string) -> std::vector<std::string>
      + derives(derived: std::string, base: std::string) -> bool
      - resolveReference(reference: bind::Reference) -> void
      - checkMessage(message: bind::Message) -> void
      - checkEvent(event: bind::Event) -> void
      - checkLocals() -> void
      - checkArtefacts() -> void
      - unifyBehaviours() -> void
      - current(id: std::string) -> std::string
      - resolveTypeText(text: std::string, scope: std::string) -> std::string
      - subjectClass(sequence: model::Entity, subject: model::Entity) -> model::Entity
      - couple(sequence: model::Entity, type: model::Entity, transient: bool) -> void
      - checkTemplateBound(reference: bind::Reference) -> void
      - checkOwnershipCycles() -> void
      - classify() -> void
    }
  }
}

diagram CL_CheckNamespace {
  kind: class
  include: driftspec@ds@check::*
  show: ownership
}
